<title>GERMANY: Eramet sees steady Russian nickel exports in 1997.</title>
<headline>Eramet sees steady Russian nickel exports in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian nickel exports to the western world in 1997 should be steady or lower compared with 140,000 tonnes of estimated exports in 1996, an official from French nickel group Eramet said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Vice president sales Francois-Gabriel Sauvage told a news conference there were no indications of major changes in the flow of Russian metal other than seasonal adjustments.</p>
<p>&quot;Domestic consumption is still low...I don't think they will be able to increase production, for which they would need help,&quot; he said in response to questions.</p>
<p>&quot;That's why export availability should be about the same as last year.&quot;</p>
</text>
